1
00:03:16,551 --> 00:03:22,551
Be careful what you wish for.

2
00:06:33,103 --> 00:06:39,103
Wish is a animation, family, fantasy film directed by Chris Buck.

3
00:09:49,655 --> 00:09:55,655
Asha, a sharp-witted idealist, makes a wish so powerful that it is answered by a
cosmic force – a little ball of boundless energy called Star.

4
00:13:06,206 --> 00:13:12,206
Together, Asha and Star confront a most formidable foe - the ruler of Rosas, King Magnifico - to save her community and prove
that when the will of one courageous human connects with the magic of the stars, wondrous things can happen.

5
00:16:22,758 --> 00:16:28,758
Asha (voice), played by Ariana DeBose.

6
00:19:39,310 --> 00:19:45,310
King Magnifico (voice), played by Chris Pine.

7
00:22:55,862 --> 00:23:01,862
Valentino (voice), played by Alan Tudyk.

8
00:26:12,413 --> 00:26:18,413
Queen Amaya (voice), played by Angelique Cabral.

9
00:29:28,965 --> 00:29:34,965
Sabino (voice), played by Victor Garber.

10
00:32:45,517 --> 00:32:51,517
Sakina (voice), played by Natasha Rothwell.

11
00:36:02,068 --> 00:36:08,068
Wish is a 2023 American animated musical fantasy film
produced by Walt Disney Animation Studios.

12
00:39:18,620 --> 00:39:24,620
It was directed by Chris Buck and Fawn Veerasunthorn and written by Jennifer Lee and Allison Moore, and stars the voices of Ariana DeBose, Chris
Pine, Alan Tudyk, Angelique Cabral, Victor Garber, Natasha Rothwell, Harvey Guillén, Evan Peters, Ramy Youssef, and Jon Rudnitsky.

13
00:42:35,172 --> 00:42:41,172
The story follows a 17-year-old girl named Asha (DeBose), who makes
a passionate plea to the stars in a moment of need.

14
00:45:51,724 --> 00:45:57,724
She meets a living, magic fallen star, and together they face the kingdom
of Rosas's devious ruler, the sorcerer Magnifico (Pine).

15
00:49:08,275 --> 00:49:14,275
Wish is inspired by Disney's centennial, tying together a
theme of most Disney films: wishes coming true.

16
00:52:24,827 --> 00:52:30,827
The film is noted to be the origin story for the "wishing star".

17
00:55:41,379 --> 00:55:47,379
The film's art style combines computer animation with
the look of traditional animation.

18
00:58:57,931 --> 00:59:03,931
Development of Wish began in 2018 but was not publicly disclosed until January 2022, when
it was revealed that Lee was writing an original film at Disney Animation.

19
01:02:14,482 --> 01:02:20,482
In September 2022, the project was officially announced, with the title
revealed alongside the involvement of DeBose and Tudyk.

20
01:05:31,034 --> 01:05:37,034
Buck and Veerasunthorn, who had worked with Lee on Frozen (2013) and Frozen II (2019) as co-director and story artist,
were confirmed as directors the same month, with Moore later hired to join Lee in writing the screenplay.

21
01:08:47,586 --> 01:08:53,586
Julia Michaels and Benjamin Rice wrote the songs, while frequent
Disney orchestrator Dave Metzger composed the score.

22
01:12:04,137 --> 01:12:10,137
Wish premiered at the El Capitan Theatre in Hollywood, Los Angeles, on November 8,
2023, and was theatrically released in the United States on November 22.

23
01:15:20,689 --> 01:15:26,689
The film received mixed reviews and grossed roughly $255 million
worldwide on a production budget of $175–200 million.

24
01:18:37,241 --> 01:18:43,241
Analysts considered it to be a box-office bomb, as the film lost the studio an estimated $131
million after accounting for income from streaming and home entertainment.

25
01:21:53,793 --> 01:21:59,793
On Disney+, it became the third most viewed premiere for a
film from Walt Disney Animation Studios.

26
01:25:10,344 --> 01:25:16,344
The film was nominated for several awards, including the
Golden Globe Award for Best Animated Feature Film.

27
01:28:26,896 --> 01:28:32,896
The film explores themes of friendship, villain, black magic, wish, musical.

28
01:31:43,448 --> 01:31:49,448
The tone is uplifting.
